{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/37","id":4686487965,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABF1YhnQ","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/37","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/37.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/37.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/37","number":37,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Record planar recurrence result and higher-dimensional gap (3009)","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# Record planar consequence and unresolved higher-dimensional gap (3009)\n\nThe complete KP-5.2 target remains unsolved. This package supplies a credited proof of the dimension-one and planar cases, including the boundary-fixed closed disk, from established Cartwright–Littlewood and Kolev–Pérouème results. The disk consequence was already stated in the 1998 paper. No discovery or full-resolution credit is claimed.\n\nThe proof explicitly checks orientation, recurrence at infinity, filled-continuum invariance, and the distinction between compact-open and Euclidean-uniform recurrence. It does not assume equicontinuity or a compact cyclic closure. The higher-dimensional homeomorphism and smooth-recurrence variants remain unresolved here.\n\nOne substantive response used; 31 exact algebraic controls pass. Separate adversarial review passed the frozen artifact with no mandatory correction; 8,462 independent exact assertions pass. The work is AI-reviewed and unrefereed. Shared queue update handled by the coordinator.\n","created_at":"2026-09-30T05:59:11Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T06:01:45Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"213df966efb4e3b1328a775af31acdc84eda4b18","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/37/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/37/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/37/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/84bb43d21b36e4d97229806e2518fbc135bee786","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:dot/math-3009","ref":"dot/math-3009","sha":"84bb43d21b36e4d97229806e2518fbc135bee786","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"http